    "result_text": "The full suite (the sole `AcceptanceTest`) is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration limit (reject with 429 once 100+ owners have been created today, by `registrationDate`), following the existing per-city capacity feature as the template so the logic lives where it belongs:\n\n- **`EnsureDailyOwnerCapacity`** (function) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals the server's current date and throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count reaches the `DAILY_LIMIT` (100). It reads the count within the write transaction, mirroring `EnsureCityHasCapacity`.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (checked escalation) \u2014 carries the offending day.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429 Too Many Requests` with a `ProblemDetail`, reusing the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper.\n- **`...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `dailyCapacity` step after the city-capacity check and before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the cap is checked before any entity is built or persisted.\n\nEach piece is a small single-responsibility unit, and shared logic (problem-detail construction) is reused rather than copied.",
